# Dual backend parity

Node.js Express is **canonical** (fully tested). Dart Shelf mirrors HTTP behaviour.

## Same PR checklist (when changing routes)

- [ ] Route path + HTTP method
- [ ] Auth / role guards
- [ ] Request body validation
- [ ] Response JSON shape
- [ ] Status codes (incl. 501 stubs)
- [ ] Calendar date fields (`YYYY-MM-DD` via `calendarDate.js` / `calendar_date.dart`)

## CI

- `dart analyze lib` on `server/` runs in CI — keep Dart routes clean.

## Known Dart gaps

Audit logging and PostHog delete are Node-only today (see `docs/technical-debt.md`).
